[10:54:20] I redrew the counterclockwise refresh arrows as a Solo48 model. `validate_icon()` returns `valid` with no warnings, and at 48 px it reads clearly as two arrows chasing each other counterclockwise.

**Construction:** it uses the suggested `CIRCLE` keyshape, which was also the best fit in the metrics (score 1.06 against 0.92 for `HRECT_L`).
- **Arcs:** each arrow is an arc of radius 15 around (24,24). The upper one runs counterclockwise from (36,15) over the top to a tip at (9,24).
- **Arrowheads:** each is an open V, `(5,19)–(9,24)–(13,19)`. Its outer arm sticks slightly outside the circle, as in the generated image, and that arm's end is the point that reaches the keyshape edge.
- **Second arrow:** the lower arrow is the upper one rotated 180° about the centre. It runs from (12,33) under the bottom to a tip at (39,24), pointing up.
- **Lucide reference:** I followed the construction of Lucide's `refresh-ccw`, two arcs with open V heads at their ends. It is the mirror image of the earlier `circular-rotating-arrows` redraw, which uses the same radius and head design and also validated.

**Changes from the trace:**
- **Shape:** the traced loop is slightly oval (about 15.8 × 15.1) with its centre near (23.8,22.9). I made it a true circle centred on the grid so every endpoint lands on whole-number points.
- **Lower arc:** the trace drew it as four curves with a kink just before the head. It is now one clean arc.
- **Arrow direction:** the heads point straight down and straight up. In the image they point a few degrees off vertical.
- **Where the arcs start:** each tail starts about 37° above or below horizontal, compared with about 23° in the image. A radius-15 circle centred on the grid has no whole-number point closer to that angle. A radius-13 circle would have one, but then a tail would sit only about 5 units from the other arrow's tip, under the minimum of 8.

**Metric issues:** the list had one item, an info note that the trace's stroke width is 2.49 after fitting where the target is 4. The new drawing is built at stroke 4. Every gap between separate parts is at least 8 units between stroke centrelines, which is the minimum; the closest is 9.5, from each tip to the start of the other arc. In the trace the closest gap was 8.34. No issues are left unfixed.

I didn't register the module, touch `published/`, or run the build or gallery updates. I made the preview PNGs with `rsvg-convert` from the model's own SVG, using a helper script at `/tmp/ccra/check.py`.

